WEBVTT

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.970
Seeking out a single ray of light,
hito-suji no hikari wo motome

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:34.210
All I can do is wander on, no matter how far.
hitasura doko made mo tada samayou

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:42.950
As I breathe a sigh not unlike surrender,
akirame ni nita tameiki wo tsuki-nagara

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:52.270
I don't want to fear how I've been hurt, all the time.
kizutsuku koto wo osoretaku nai yo itsu mo

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.650
Set me free now!

00:00:54.670 --> 00:01:01.060
Come on, let it all go, to the far reaches of time,
saa tokihanate subete toki no kanata ni

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:01.080
From that which binds the soul!
tamashii wo shibaru mono wo

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:06.910
tamashii wo shibaru mono wo
From that which binds the soul!

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.200
For my heartbeat!

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.690
Make freedom your weapon,
jiyuu wo buki ni

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:11.760
And you are sure to attain it!
kitto te ni ireru no yo

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.470
kitto te ni ireru no yo
And you are sure to attain it!

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:15.510
The power to believe and dream is there
shinjiru chikara wo yume wo

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:21.590
shinjiru chikara wo yume wo
The power to believe and dream is there

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:21.630
for you to go on living.
ikite yuku tame ni

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:25.960
ikite yuku tame ni
for you to go on living.

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:02.630
It's quiet... Almost as if everything has gone to sleep.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:06.400
Don't you think so, Yuji?

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:09.210
Yuji...?

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.380
Yuji?

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.720
What is it, Marlene? Have you detected any Blue?

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:24.730
No.

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:27.390
You're looking forward to the Blue that much?

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:29.730
What's that?

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:33.230
Nothing. Don't worry about it.

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:38.340
They're coming!

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:39.810
Blue approaching!

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.010
Let's go, Marlene!

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:51.050
Yeah!

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:25.380
It's begun.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:30.050
Aw! I wanted to support Yuji in the city.

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:34.650
You should probably give that up. You'd just hold Yuji back.

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:36.320
How nice of you to say so.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.960
Save the chit-chat until after the mission is completed.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:48.000
The target Nest is 20 kilos ahead. Stay sharp.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.100
Copy. Once the Nest is destroyed,

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.340
we'll head for the rendezvous point immediately.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:01.350
A detached force?

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:04.690
Are you seriously saying this? A diversionary mission?

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:10.030
Yes. If we're to arrive at the return shuttle departure point on time,

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.590
this Nest is in the way.

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:14.790
But if we were to detour around it,

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:18.360
we will not make it to the shuttle in time. Right?

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:23.670
As I draw the Blue out, everyone else take out the Nest. By doing so,

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:26.040
we can all get back to Second Earth together.

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:29.880
You make it sound so simple. I guess we should expect that from a Sleeper.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:39.660
It certainly is an interesting mission...

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:41.990
As he is now, Yuji can't handle it.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.330
- Tony!
- Wait!

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:52.340
If you like, how about we let this decide?

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:57.570
Heads, Yuji diverts them, tails, I do.

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:01.050
You got it.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:18.700
It's heads! Yuji wins!

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:27.540
Don't die, now.

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:47.420
Yuji!

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:50.920
Why, you...!

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.410
You okay?

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:09.010
Yeah.

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:14.680
Still, you're completely overworked.
At this pace, your own body will also...

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:16.350
You mind your own business!

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:20.690
I was the one who proposed this mission! I absolutely must not fail!

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:23.700
I can do it as well!

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:24.990
Yuji!

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:50.660
Marlene...

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:55.320
It's wondrous, isn't it? Even with this many humans gone,

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:59.130
the Earth continues to live on, unchanged.

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:09.010
Wait, Yuji!

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:10.670
Children?

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:51.320
There are no more Blue around here. Let's go.

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:56.980
Not very charming. He has no sense of cooperation, huh?

00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:00.650
Alicia, no more chatter. We're still on the mission.

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:01.790
Phooey...

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:18.000
Impossible... how can there be people in a jungle like this?

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.380
Is there any one else around?

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:28.350
Marlene,

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:30.410
don't split up! We're on a mission!

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:39.130
I'm a friend.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:47.440
A friend.

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:59.280
Are there any other people? If there are, would you tell me where they are?

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:03.980
I see.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.420
Yuji, let's go.

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:13.000
Don't interfere!

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:17.390
It's them!

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:38.330
Marlene!

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:02.980
Wait! Don't get separated! It's dangerous!

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:04.640
Yuji! The children!

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:05.710
Shut up!

00:10:09.390 --> 00:10:10.760
Move it!

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:16.320
Stop it.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:19.330
Stop it, Yuji! There are still people here!

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:22.490
Stay out of the way!

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:25.170
Yuji!

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:30.710
What's that?

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.450
The Blue Nest has been completely pacified.

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:48.290
There is no sign of the existence of any potentially active Blue.

00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:54.300
It's over at last! I want to take a shower and freshen up right away!

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:57.100
Reporting our unit's current status.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:59.400
Casualties: 0; Damaged vehicles: 0;

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:02.170
Remaining ammunition: 90% or better in each rig;

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:04.580
Remaining power: 90% or better.

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:29.660
The mission is concluded without incident. Hastening to the rendezvous point.

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:31.530
Copy. Yuji's unit,

00:11:31.610 --> 00:11:35.670
break off mission actions at once and hurry to the rendezvous point.

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:37.010
No way!

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:38.010
Marlene?

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:42.020
There are still people surviving in these woods!

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:43.310
Marlene!

00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:38.770
You goddamn bug!

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:01.520
Yuji!

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:04.090
You bastard!

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:17.540
Now to finish you!

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:12.690
Say, looks like our unit's the only one that had no one hurt.

00:14:12.770 --> 00:14:15.530
Now, when it clears tomorrow, we can return to Second Earth.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:18.370
All thanks to Tony and Yuji.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:21.200
These Sleepers were really something.

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:30.380
Don't be jealous of them. They're different from us.

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:31.980
Different?

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:35.820
Sure they are, those of us raised on Second Earth.

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:39.330
Just so long as we do well here, you know?

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:43.990
What are you talking about?

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:48.660
About how you at least will always be one of our friends.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:54.680
How's that? Oof! Time to change the watch. Don't let us down.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.210
Yeah, yeah.

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:04.650
Yuji's not around. Say, say, how was Yuji today?

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:12.650
He's so cool, you know? Yuji! Don't you think?

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:19.700
After all, to think he would go on that diversionary mission by himself...

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:24.640
Tony is also definitely awesome, but there's nothing cute about him.

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:29.110
If I were to pick a boyfriend, it would definitely be Yuji.

00:15:35.050 --> 00:15:38.950
I really like a strong man.

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:43.660
No.

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:48.180
That... isn't the real Yuji.

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:56.730
What do you mean, the real Yuji? I only know the Yuji there is now.

00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:04.410
Aah, Marlene, you're jealous of Yuji.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:09.010
As a soldier, you wanted to always be better than him. That's it, isn't it?

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:12.020
No, it isn't.

00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:17.680
That's not it. I... I...

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:20.230
Marlene?

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:30.700
What's she getting all serious for? It's worth it to tease her. Yow!

00:16:48.390 --> 00:16:50.290
What are you doing?

00:16:52.390 --> 00:16:55.660
Confirming our return schedule to Second Earth.

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:58.260
I do not want us to be late.

00:17:29.760 --> 00:17:31.250
Marlene...

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:41.970
It's great that you're so dedicated, but is it okay for you to not get any rest?

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:46.000
If I could handle this thing a little better... if I could tune in better...

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:51.310
this thing's performance should be higher.

00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:52.320
I see...

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:23.350
Yuji, how do you suppose those children are doing now?

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:27.010
Do you suppose they lived through all that safely?

00:18:27.090 --> 00:18:29.680
There's no helping them.

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:34.960
If we are to exterminate the Blue, that is something we can't do anything about.

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:39.630
Besides, eventually, they were to have been killed by the Blue anyhow.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:42.290
A- are you seriously saying that?

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:46.310
If I let myself be distracted by such things, I won't catch up to him.

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:51.310
This is nothing near the Blue that he has killed.

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:53.310
Those marks...

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:58.880
If only I were stronger, had more power... then even Tony would...

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:07.320
The Blue are raiding! It's the Blue!

00:19:15.740 --> 00:19:16.730
Let's go!

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:51.960
This is the real thing at last!

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:56.980
Their situations are indisputably advancing. Just as we speculated.

00:19:57.040 --> 00:20:00.640
Yes. We are moving on to the next step.

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:04.080
The day when we can return to Earth is near.

00:21:30.050 --> 00:21:39.540
Although the days when we smiled again and again
hohoemi kasaneta hibi ga

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:45.670
Have passed away into dreams,
maboroshi ni natte mo

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:54.820
I will surely not lose my way.
watashi wa kitto mayowanai

00:21:54.940 --> 00:22:00.990
To go on to the future,
mirai ni yuku tame ni

00:22:01.140 --> 00:22:07.410
To become an adult,
otona ni naru tame ni

00:22:07.770 --> 00:22:14.600
I again recall now the memories
mogaite kita omoide wo kokoro de

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:19.760
twisting in my heart.
ima wa kurikaesu

00:22:19.860 --> 00:22:25.820
I'm living in one time,
hitotsu no toki wo iki

00:22:26.120 --> 00:22:32.100
While choosing two dreams,
futatsu no yume erabi

00:22:32.710 --> 00:22:39.580
And love taught me what it means...
soshite ai ga oshiete kureta yo ne

00:22:39.760 --> 00:22:46.440
to cherish someone.
hito wo omou imi

00:22:50.120 --> 00:22:53.380
Oh, are you still at it, Yuji?

00:22:53.460 --> 00:22:58.390
Finally, I've caught up with you! I'm not about to be left behind alone!

00:22:58.460 --> 00:23:00.160
A Sample for data purposes...

00:23:00.230 --> 00:23:05.060
a comrade's existence not being omitted - the environment has already changed!

00:23:05.130 --> 00:23:11.070
Why is that man keeping me here...? Or is it...

00:23:11.140 --> 00:23:13.400
Wait! Yuji!
